<title>UK: EIB sets 20 bln escudo-into-euro 10-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>EIB sets 20 bln escudo-into-euro 10-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank has launched a 20 billion escudo Eurobond due February 2007 which may be redenominated in euros after the third stage of EMU, lead manager Banco CISF said on Thursday. The deal carries a 5.75 percent coupon and was priced at 95.322 with 2.45 points fees.  </p>
<p>If redenominated in euros, the notes will be fungible with two other outstanding issues -- for 1.0 billion guilders and 3.0 billion French francs -- launched by the EIB earlier this year, and possible unspecified future issues.  </p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT     20 BLN PTE   COUPON     5.75	MATURITY    15.FEB.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  95.322    PAY DATE    26.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.45	LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS     **	  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> NOTES    **100K-1M-10M-50M</p>
